# Local experiments

Do not run probes, comparisons, or one-off tests from `/tmp`, and do not write their scripts or results there.

Put the script in `tools/` at the repo root, in the directory for its subject. A one-off trial goes in `tools/trials/`. A file typed by hand that a script reads goes beside that script.

Put the output in `scratch/` at the repo root. Create that directory if it is missing. `scratch/` is for temporary output only: files a script can make again. It is gitignored, so the output can stay on disk for inspection without being committed. Do not put a script in `scratch/`.

The speech path and the unit tests stay as they are until a trial is kept. A result that is discarded leaves its output in `scratch/` rather than disappearing with the temp directory.

```text
# Bad
/tmp/probe_syllable_pause.py
scratch/syllable-pause.py

# Good
tools/trials/syllable-pause.py
scratch/syllable-pause.txt
```
